.TH DOMESTIKOS 1 "August 2026" "excubitor @VERSION@" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
domestikos \- admin commands for excubitor, the GPU lock manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B domestikos
.I command
.RI [ options "] ..."
.br
.B domestikos
.RB { \-h | \-\-help }
.br
.B domestikos
.RB { \-v | \-\-version }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B domestikos
is the admin\-only counterpart to
.BR excubitor (1),
named after the Domestikos ton Exkoubiton, the Byzantine officer who
commanded the excubitores palace guard. Unless noted otherwise, its
commands must be run as root.
.PP
It owns the things a regular user cannot do: force\-clearing another
user's stale lock/meta files (never a lock still held by a live
process \(em there is no force\-eviction of running jobs), and
periodically enforcing GPU compute mode plus checking for
.B excubitor
bypass usage.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gc
Force\-clear stale (dead\-process) lock/meta files, for any user \(em
the sticky bit on
.I LOCK_DIR
otherwise blocks a regular user from clearing anyone else's. Never
touches a lock still held by a live process. Requires root.
.TP
.B status
Same view as
.BR "excubitor status" .
.TP
.B check
Best\-effort (re\-)assert
.B "nvidia\-smi \-c EXCLUSIVE_PROCESS"
on every GPU, then log a WARN line for any bypass found:
.RS
.IP \(bu 3
a GPU
.B excubitor
considers free but the driver shows in use;
.IP \(bu 3
a GPU
.B excubitor
considers locked that the driver shows in use by someone other than the
lock holder;
.IP \(bu 3
a GPU whose actual compute mode isn't
.BR EXCLUSIVE_PROCESS ,
since the reassert above gives no feedback either way \(em this is the
only way to notice it didn't take, e.g. because it was blocked by a
process already holding a context in some other mode.
.RE
.IP
WARN lines are visible via
.BR "domestikos offenders" " or " "journalctl \-u domestikos.service" .
Run periodically by
.BR domestikos.timer ;
safe to run by hand any time. Requires root.
.TP
.RI "offenders [" since ]
Show
.BR check 's
bypass warnings from the systemd journal.
.I since
is any
.BR journalctl (1)
.B \-\-since
value (default: "24 hours ago"). Does not require root.
.TP
.RI "usage [" since ]
Per\-user job count and total GPU\-time, aggregated from the USAGE
records
.B excubitor run
logs to the journal (tag
.IR excubitor )
each time a job releases its GPU(s).
.I since
is any
.BR journalctl (1)
.B \-\-since
value (default: "7 days ago"). Reading other users' journal entries
typically requires root or
.B systemd\-journal
group membership, so in practice this is an admin\-only view even
though the command itself doesn't enforce it.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage. Also available per\-command, e.g.
.BR "domestikos check \-h" .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the installed version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IR /var/lock/excubitor/gpu<N>.lock ", " gpu<N>.meta
Per\-GPU lock/metadata files; see
.BR excubitor (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
domestikos check
domestikos offenders "1 hour ago"
domestikos usage "30 days ago"
sudo domestikos gc
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR excubitor (1),
.BR nvidia\-smi (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.SH BUGS
Report problems to the administrators via the "FCC SW Machines"
Mattermost channel: https://mattermost.web.cern.ch/fccsw/channels/fccsw-machines
